  "description": "<p>As reported on the dev list, if a dc element in the DC datastream contains an xml:lang attribute (e.g. \"&lt;dc:subject xml:lang=\"da\"&gt;Tidsinterval&lt;/dc:subject&gt;\"), the xml:lang attribute is dropped during ingest.</p>\n\n<p>Additionally, the xml:lang attribute is not dropped if the DC datastream is added via addDatastream.</p>\n\n<p>This was reported against 3.0b1, but I believe this affects all versions of Fedora.</p>",
